Cyrus is sitting at his writing desk, looking at maps of some lands. Having noticed you coming through the door, he put them aside.
"Mr. Cyrus, do you happen to have the map of Wild Island?" you ask.
"I had it somewhere," he answers, "let's look for it".
You kept searching for quite a long time, in spite of the fact, that everyone was trying to help. Alas, a sheet of parchment that was found disappointed you. The map is incomplete, and was not of much benefit to you.
"Chin up Henry!" Cyrus consoles you, "look what I found!"
He holds a massive spyglass in his hands. It consists of two black cylinders, belted by copper rings. Lenses are gleaming dimly.
"I thought, I had lost it long time ago!" he smiled, "Well, since we found it thanks to you, take it, it's yours!"
Such a present has improved your mood, and now you say goodbye to Cyrus and go to the exit.